From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:02:59 +0200
Subject: threads: background threads at nice 10 on Linux, the render thread
 first (LU_NICE)

Map generation (Emerge-N), meshing (MeshUpdate), the built-in server,
the minimap and the async Lua workers prepare work for later frames;
the render thread draws this one. On the PS3's two hardware threads,
at viewing range 120, these threads and kswapd kept both busy, and in
the frames over 100 ms the render thread ran only about a fifth of the
time (perf samples against the stall recorder's frames). At nice 10
the scheduler runs the render thread whenever it is ready, and the
background work is done in its gaps.

LU_NICE=N sets the value, LU_NICE=0 leaves the threads as upstream.

Forwarded: not-needed

diff --git a/src/threading/thread.cpp b/src/threading/thread.cpp
--- a/src/threading/thread.cpp
+++ b/src/threading/thread.cpp
@@ -44,6 +44,14 @@ DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.
 	};
 #endif
 
+// for the background threads' priority (LU_NICE)
+#if defined(__linux__)
+	#include <cstdlib>
+	#include <sys/resource.h>
+	#include <sys/syscall.h>
+	#include <unistd.h>
+#endif
+
 // for bindToProcessor
 #if __FreeBSD_version >= 702106
 	typedef cpuset_t cpu_set_t;
@@ -184,6 +192,26 @@ void Thread::threadProc(Thread *thr)
 
 	thr->setName(thr->m_name);
 
+#if defined(__linux__)
+	// Walnut (PS3): the threads that only prepare work for later (map generation, meshing, the
+	// built-in server, the minimap, async Lua) run at nice LU_NICE (default 10; 0 or unset by
+	// "LU_NICE=0": as upstream). With two hardware threads and four busy threads, the render
+	// thread otherwise waits its turn: at viewing range 120 it ran a fifth of the time in its
+	// frames over 100 ms. Linux keeps a nice value per thread, and raising one's own needs no
+	// privilege; the work still gets done, in the render thread's gaps.
+	{
+		static const int bg_nice = [] {
+			const char *v = getenv("LU_NICE");
+			return v && *v ? atoi(v) : 10;
+		}();
+		const std::string &n = thr->m_name;
+		const bool background = n == "MeshUpdate" || n == "MinimapUpdate" || n == "Server" ||
+			n.rfind("Emerge-", 0) == 0 || n.rfind("AsyncWorker-", 0) == 0;
+		if (background && bg_nice > 0)
+			setpriority(PRIO_PROCESS, (id_t)syscall(SYS_gettid), bg_nice);
+	}
+#endif
+
 	g_logger.registerThread(thr->m_name);
 	thr->m_running = true;
 
